    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im looking into some stuff for a project in london. we're comparing signalized intersections vs roundabouts for a major junction. can you explain the main differences in terms of traffic throughput and how they handle peak hour flow?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Signalized intersections prioritize phases allowing controlled, systematic movement, whereas roundabouts use continuous flow regulated by driver yield. Generally, roundabouts can handle higher traffic volumes with less delay during peak hours because they eliminate the waiting time associated with traffic lights. However, signalized junctions offer greater predictability and control, which can be advantageous when complex turning movements must be strictly ordered. The best choice depends heavily on the specific traffic demand patterns and geometric layout of the junction.",
      "source": "target",
